-- REFUSED: `MAYBE NUMBER` (R8).
-- An unanswered docassemble number field submits as 0/0.0, never None
-- (views.py coercion, spec §8.6), so "absent" is indistinguishable from a
-- real answer of zero. MAYBE NUMBER (and MAYBE DATE) are therefore refused
-- by name in v1, pending the M4 paired is-known question design.
-- MAYBE BOOLEAN and MAYBE STRING are fine — see ../defaults.l4.
-- The file itself typechecks: the refusal belongs to `l4 docassemble`.

DECLARE Claim
    HAS
      @desc Income the claimant declared, if any was declared at all
      `declared income` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

@export Whether the claimant declared income above the reporting threshold
GIVEN c IS A Claim @desc The claim under assessment
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `declared income exceeds threshold` c IF
    CONSIDER c's `declared income`
    WHEN JUST n  THEN n GREATER THAN 1000
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

#EVAL `declared income exceeds threshold` (Claim WITH `declared income` IS JUST 2500)  -- TRUE
#EVAL `declared income exceeds threshold` (Claim WITH `declared income` IS NOTHING)   -- FALSE
